-## Next
+## Latest acceptance-suite failure
+
+Browser acceptance suite reports a `removeChild` crash on editing test
+"should remove the item if an empty text string was entered".
+Root cause: three interacting defects in the edit-destroy flow:
+
+1. `destroyTodo` calls `render()` internally — every caller also calls `render()`
+   afterwards, producing a double-render that removes the `<li>` from DOM twice.
+   The in-harness happy-dom does not reproduce the crash because its
+   `querySelectorAll` returns a fresh static node list on each call, so the
+   second call to `removeChild` on an already-removed `<li>` is simply a no-op
+   (the `<li>` is not in the list). A real browser keeps a live DOM reference.
 
-Dispatch QM on the watchbill (watch1-watch7). Context MUST clear before QM.
+2. The edit keydown Enter handler calls `self.save()` and `self.render()` after
+   `destroyTodo` returns, even though `destroyTodo` already did both.
 
-## DOM-identity defect
+3. The edit blur handler (capture-phase on `.todo-list`) calls `destroyTodo` for
+   empty input without guarding against the keydown handler having already
+   destroyed the todo. In a real browser, pressing Enter on the edit input
+   fires blur (because the `<li>` leaves the DOM, which moves focus). The blur
+   handler's `input.closest('li')` returns the detached `<li>`, and the
+   subsequent `destroyTodo` → `render` → `removeChild` fails because the node
+   is no longer in the DOM tree.
 
-The `render()` function in `js/app.js` destroys and recreates all `<li>` elements on every state
-toggle (`list.innerHTML = ''` followed by `createElement('li')` per todo). This causes Cypress
-to lose references (detached-from-DOM errors) on 4 acceptance-suite scenarios:
-- mark-all toggle/uncheck
-- single-item complete/uncomplete
+## Fix required
 
-The in-harness happy-dom tier does not reproduce this because it re-queries the DOM fresh after
-each action. There are 2 pre-existing harness failures unrelated to this defect:
-1. toggle-all checkbox checks when all become checked
-2. first item not completed on reload
+Three conformance scenarios in `features/conformance.feature` pin the fix:
+- `destroyTodo` must not call `render` or `save` (callers own rendering)
+- The edit keydown Enter handler must not call `save` or `render` after `destroyTodo`
+- The edit blur handler must guard against model-absent todo before calling `destroyTodo`
+
+The product scenario `features/todos.feature:Saving an empty title deletes the todo`
+already describes the correct behaviour.
+
+## Next
 
-`features/conformance.feature` (watch7) pins the required fix: the `toggleTodo` and toggle-all
-handler MUST mutate existing DOM nodes in-place (classList.toggle, checkbox.checked) and MUST
-NOT call `render()`. Crew will implement the product fix; these conformance scenarios will
-then pass when QM runs the bespoke checker.
